      "body": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "I always download mine as mark down and save it locally.",
                "type": "text",
                "circle_ios_fallback_text": "I always download mine as mark down and save it locally."
              },
              {
                "type": "hardBreak",
                "circle_ios_fallback_text": "\n"
              },
              {
                "text": "If I need to change something I usually open a new chat (or the existing) depending on what I need or want, copy my existing one and prompt it so I can create the necessary changes in a conversation mode. Then it creates a new artifact which I replace the old one with. Not sure if this is the most efficient one but it works for me, as I A) want to make sure I have all the information stored (locally) and not somewhere lost in a conversation with AI and B) I can directly work with my latest artifact (even if I’d switch the AI model for example). Hope it helps.",
                "type": "text",
                "circle_ios_fallback_text": "If I need to change something I usually open a new chat (or the existing) depending on what I need or want, copy my existing one and prompt it so I can create the necessary changes in a conversation mode. Then it creates a new artifact which I replace the old one with. Not sure if this is the most efficient one but it works for me, as I A) want to make sure I have all the information stored (locally) and not somewhere lost in a conversation with AI and B) I can directly work with my latest artifact (even if I’d switch the AI model for example). Hope it helps."
              }
            ]
          }
